# Architecture

- Use the modern Next.js App Router.
- Prefer Server Components unless client-side interactivity is genuinely required.
- Use `use client` only when needed.
- Prefer server-side data access for protected/private operations.
- Use Route Handlers or Server Actions only where appropriate.
- Keep UI, data access, validation and business logic reasonably separated.
- Reuse existing utilities/components before creating new ones.
- Do not introduce a state-management library unless the project genuinely requires it.
- Do not rewrite working architecture without a clear reason.
- Keep the application practical for cPanel + Node.js deployment.
